<article class="env-lemma" id="09LT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09LT">Lemma <span data-tag="09LT">22.33.5</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $(A, \text{d})$ and $(B, \text{d})$ be differential graded $R$-algebras. Let $N$ be a differential graded $(A, B)$-bimodule. Then the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  - \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} N : D(A, \text{d}) \longrightarrow D(B, \text{d})  \]
</div>
  <p> of Lemma <a href="/tag/09LS" data-tag="09LS">22.33.2</a> is a left adjoint to the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (N, -) : D(B, \text{d}) \longrightarrow D(A, \text{d})  \]
</div>
  <p> of Lemma <a href="/tag/09LI" data-tag="09LI">22.31.2</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FND" data-tag="0FND">13.30.1</a> and the fact that $- \otimes _ A N$ and $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\text{Mod}^{dg}_{(B, \text{d})}}(N, -)$ are adjoint by Lemma <a href="/tag/09LN" data-tag="09LN">22.30.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>